{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py","reason":"hosts the write-temp-then-os.replace atomic-replace idiom; POSIX permits replacing a file another handle has open, Windows enforces mandatory locking and raises PermissionError [WinError 32], so the atomicity guarantee the callers assume does not hold as written"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/ensures.py","reason":"another os.replace site in the store path; same mandatory-locking exposure"},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py","reason":"replaces and unlinks snapshot files that readers may still hold open; WinError 5 'Access is denied' and the FileNotFoundError cluster in the sweep sit in this neighbourhood"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_compact_crash_atomicity.py","reason":"16 failures; the crash-atomicity oracle that must prove the replace guarantee holds on Windows rather than being satisfied by closing handles in teardown"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_compact_all_selection.py","reason":"17 failures, the 6th-largest failing file; exercises the same compaction replace path"}]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1788571572449431081,"uuid":"09489792-ade3-4eb4-811f-63e6bf44f85e"}